# The install scripts are run by bash on the server. A CRLF slipping into one
# of them turns every line into a syntax error there, and the failure ("$'\r':
# command not found") gives no hint of the cause — so line endings are pinned
# rather than left to whatever the contributor's editor does.
* text=auto eol=lf

scripts/* text eol=lf
conf/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
